8: /**
9:  * Canary sweep with a positive control (privacy suite design, issue #25 section 3; A7 part b).
10:  *
11:  *   node infra/tests/privacy/canary-sweep.ts --stage pr-12 https://pr-12.app.surveybeat.app https://pr-12.submit.surveybeat.app
12:  *
13:  * 1. Sends a unique canary to the Main Worker (logs on) and another to the Submission Worker (logs off),
14:  *    each REQUESTS times, because the account samples Workers Logs (see `observability.ts`).
15:  * 2. Positive control: polls Workers Logs for up to 10 minutes until the Main Worker's canary is found.
16:  *    Without this, zero hits for the Submission Worker would prove nothing.
17:  * 3. Only then: the Submission Worker produced zero events, and its canary appears in no event of any Worker.
18:  *
19:  * Today the sweep covers Workers Logs. The other sinks (Analytics Engine, Queue and dead-letter messages,
20:  * R2 backups, a D1 dump, response bodies) join as the slices that write to them land.
21:  * Needs CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN (Workers Observability read) and CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID.
22:  */
